@ulikemyname6744 What nonsense are you talking about? Byd has been selling cars for 20 years before Tesla was born. How can Tesla's supply chain compare with byd. What's MORE important is that byd was originally a battery company! BYD may be the ONLY automobile company in the WORLD that produces all vehicle parts in-house. Many of Tesla's batteries are imported from expensive Japan. Recently, he also imported new blade batteries from BYD for his new car. How can the two be compared in terms of cost? ? 
If BYD had any separate subsidies, it would have been hyped thousands of times by Western media. Do they still need you to make it up here?
Moreover, the product itself also has problems with brand premium and target profit margin setting. BYD has never been a premium brand in the past 20 years, but Tesla has been since its birth. If it weren't for the challenge from China's electric cars, Tesla's price would be several times more expensive, and it wouldn't produce a cost-squeezing model like Model 3.

@XkMeng You think a company needs 20 years to establish reliable supply chain? Spoiler alert, you don't! Tesla is the most vertically integrated company in the world! More than BYD! And no, BYD is not producing 100% in-house. Hard to believe Nvidia is a subsidiary of BYD because BYD uses Nvidia semiconductors and semiconductors from a whole bunch of other companies. 

Tesla is producing their batteries themselves for the most part. Every factory of Tesla has a part specifically made to produce batteries. Panasonic is one of the producers but within Tesla's own factories meaning that they import expertise. So, Tesla is effectively self-sufficient. Now they were forced to cooperate with CATL in China and some other Chinese suppliers for their cheap models because Tesla is selling a lot of cars and the growth rates are still high. 

Yes, BYD is subsidies and not just them but many Chinese EV makers. For example Nio. A company that's barely even growing is somehow losing tens of thousands of dollars for every vehicle they sell? Which bank exactly is lending them money? When Tesla was losing that much on cars, their sales were growing like there was no tomorrow. Nio is barely growing and they are somehow good for loans? Yeah, sure bud! The idea is Chinese domination of the market. The same exact thing they did with Huawei and their telecom equipment. They same thing they do with every high-priority technology

